INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(6700, 0, 67, 0, 0, 13, 'The Storm Peaks', 'The Storm Peaks rise in the northeast of Northrend, a realm of wind-scoured summits, glaciers and frozen valleys, and the highest mountain in Northrend is crowned by the open-sided Temple of Storms. This was the domain of the titans'' keepers. At its northern edge stands Ulduar, a titan city of vast halls and terraces, now held by Loken, whose iron dwarves make war on every creature of stone and have driven the earthen from their home. Elsewhere the old pacts lie broken. The frost giants of Dun Niffelem, the Sons of Hodir, feud with the Hyldnir, the vrykul women of Brunnhildar who serve the brooding Thorim, while their sisters at Valkyrion have taken the Lich King''s gift. Strangers have come as well: goblin prospectors at K3, the Explorers'' League among the frost dwarves of Frosthold, a stranded Horde zeppelin crew at Grom''arsh, and Brann Bronzebeard, chasing the secrets of Ulduar.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Storm_Peaks (northeastern Northrend, highest mountain topped by the open-sided Temple of Storms, keepers, Ulduar); quests 12885, 12929 (Loken expelled the earthen from Ulduar; iron dwarves'' campaign against the creatures of stone); npc_text 13778-13779 (Thorim; war between the Hyldnir and the Sons of Hodir); quests 12942, 12925 (Valkyrion accepted the Lich King; val''kyr); quest 12853 reward text (K3 goblins after the titan machines); quests 12862, 12871 (Explorers'' League at Frosthold), 12895, 13000 (the crashed Horde zeppelin); quest 12854 (Brann''s search)'),
(6701, 1, 67, 1, 0, 13, 'K3', 'K3 is a goblin town at the southern foot of the Storm Peaks, built by prospectors who came for their share of the titan machines hidden in the mountains. Progress has been slow: the cold freezes the motor of every flier they launch, and trouble presses on every side. Savage Hill gnolls under Gnarlhide steal parts from the town''s very doorstep, Tore Rumblewrench''s miners have still to clear Crystalweb Cavern of its spiders, and to the northeast the magnataur of Garm and their snobold followers mean to take K3 for themselves. West of town lies Jeer Sparksocket''s minefield, watched over by turrets that shoot down anything trying to fly in.', 'quest 12853 reward text (came for the titan machines; fliers'' motors freeze; gnolls, snobolds, magnataur); quest 12836 description (Gnarlhide''s gnolls stealing parts on the doorstep); quests 12829, 12830 (Tore, Crystalweb Cavern spiders); quest 12820 description (magnataur keen to take K3; defenses and laser turrets northeast); quest 12821 description (sapper squad); zone_areas 4418-4462 (K3, Snowblind Hills, Garm, Garm''s Bane, Garm''s Rise, Sparksocket Minefield, Ricket''s Folly); quest 12819 description (Jeer''s minefield in the west; turrets shoot down fliers)'),
(6702, 1, 67, 2, 0, 13, 'Sifreldar Village and the Forlorn Mine', 'Sifreldar Village looks down on K3 from the heights to the north, a settlement of the Hyldnir, the frost vrykul women of the peaks, guarded by storm maidens and runekeepers. Rusty cages hold goblin prisoners and salvaged K3 equipment lies among the longhouses, for the Hyldnir fell on a goblin expedition climbing into the mountains to raise a transmission tower, carried off its men and let the women go. In the north of the village is the entrance to the Forlorn Mine, where captive vrykul men dig under the blades of Hyldnir overseers.', 'quest 12843 description (expedition to set up a transmission tower; blue, frost-layered vrykul women; took the men, let the women go; Sifreldar overlooks K3); quest 12844 description (equipment taken; village to the north); quest 12846 description (mine in northern Sifreldar where they work prisoners); quest 12906 description (male vrykul work the mines out of fear of the blades); zone_areas 4423: Sifreldar Storm Maiden, Runekeeper, Goblin Prisoner, Rusty Cage, K3 Equipment'),
(6703, 1, 67, 3, 0, 13, 'Brunnhildar Village', 'Brunnhildar Village is the stronghold of the Hyldnir, who call themselves the servants of Thorim. Here the women rule and fight, and they hold that whoever wins the Hyldsmeet, their sacred contest of strength, is assured a lifetime at Thorim''s side. Challengers spar in the lanes, bear riders school their warbears for the Pit of the Fang, and proto-drakes are kept for the riders of the sky. The Hyldnir are at war with the frost giants of Dun Niffelem, beyond the Valley of Ancient Winters, and they meet any outsider who walks into the village with steel.', 'npc_text 13540 (the Hyldsmeet is sacred; victory assures a lifetime next to Thorim); npc_text 13843 (we serve Thorim); quest 12970 description (the Hyldsmeet); quest 12972 description (feud with the Sons of Hodir); quest 12997 (Pit of the Fang); zone_areas 4422 (Brunnhildar Challenger, Bearhandler, Riding Bear, Hyldsmeet Proto-Drake); faction templates 2109/2113 hostile to all players'),
(6704, 1, 67, 4, 0, 13, 'Valkyrion', 'Valkyrion lies far to the northwest, beyond the Temple of Storms, a Hyldnir village that turned from Thorim. Its people accepted the advances of the Lich King, and those who receive his gift, the val''kyr, fly above the village on feathered wings. Rather than capture their drakes in the wild as their sisters do, the aspirants of Valkyrion raise them from blight: the eggs lie in a fetid pool of plague, and blighted proto-drakes hatch from them. In the largest dwelling lives Yulda the Stormspeaker, the witch who carried the Lich King''s promises of power to Brunnhildar.', 'quest 12942 description (Valkyrion northwest beyond the Temple of Storms; the Lich King''s gift; val''kyr on feathered wings); quest 12925 description (accepted the Scourge''s advances; drakes raised from blight; fetid pool of blight); quest 12968 description (Yulda, largest dwelling, the Lich King''s promises); zone_areas 4424/4499: Nascent Val''kyr, Valkyrion Aspirant, Blighted Proto-Drake, Plagued Proto-Drake Egg, Yulda 30046'),
(6705, 1, 67, 5, 0, 13, 'Temple of Storms', 'The Temple of Storms stands open to the winds on the summit of the highest mountain in Northrend, and within it sits Thorim, the Stormlord, alone. He has withdrawn here from the world below and broods in silence, heedless of those who climb to him. Around the peak wheel the proto-drakes of the Hyldnir, their wild kin nest across the Dragonspine Peaks, and on a lesser peak to the southeast lies the Broodmother''s Nest, long empty of eggs.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Storm_Peaks (Temple of Storms, open-sided, highest mountain); npc_text 13779 (Thorim exiled himself to the Temple of Storms); quest 12886 completion text (Begone!); quest 13050 description (old empty nest); zone_areas 4430 (Thorim 29445, Hyldsmeet Proto-Drake x21), 4433 (Stormpeak Hatchlings), 4631'),
(6706, 1, 67, 6, 0, 13, 'Frosthold', 'Frosthold lies in a great pit of ice atop a mountain in the southwest of the peaks, the stronghold of the frostborn, the frost dwarves. They are a warrior people ruled by King Yorg Stormheart, and the stormcrest eagles that nest on the heights above the town are their old allies and their mounts. An Explorers'' League expedition under Lagnus has made camp among them, its archaeologists and relic hunters welcomed by their hosts. In the valleys of Bor''s Breath to the east, Frostfeather harpies harry the frostborn and their eagles alike.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Frosthold (pit of ice atop a mountain, southwestern Storm Peaks, home of the frostborn); npc_text 13733 (Fjorlin: eagles our allies for longer than I''ve walked the land); quest 12869 (riding a Stormcrest Eagle); quest 12863 description (how welcoming the frostborn have been); zone_areas 4428 (Lagnus, Andorin, Rork Sharpchin of the Explorers'' League; Yorg Stormheart 29593; Stormcrest Eagles); quests 12864, 12866, 12867 (harpies of Bor''s Breath valley; eagle eggs; scouts)'),
(6707, 1, 67, 7, 0, 13, 'Grom''arsh Crash-Site', 'The Grom''arsh Crash-Site is a Horde camp raised in the wreck of a goblin zeppelin that came down high in the peaks, and its crew has stayed where it fell. Boktar Bloodfury commands here, with the shaman Moteha Windborn and Bloodguard Lorga among his people, and a few grunts keep watch over the broken hull. The cold is the camp''s worst enemy, and the crew burns timbers from the wreck to stay alive. Worgs make their lair in Gimorak''s Den, a cave east of the camp.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Grom''arsh_Crash-Site (camp in the wreck of a goblin zeppelin); quest 12910 description (Boktar in command); quest 13000 description (wood from the wreckage burned for warmth; worg cave to the east); zone_areas 4429 (Boktar 29651, Moteha 29937, Lorga 30247, Warsong Hold Grunts)'),
(6708, 1, 67, 8, 0, 13, 'The Foot Steppes and the Engine of the Makers', 'The Foot Steppes are hard, open land east of Frosthold, where ice rhinos graze and proto-drakes hunt among the crags. Stormforged trackers prowl them, and in the southeast the Frigid Tomb is held by ancient guardians of ice. In the midst of the steppes the Engine of the Makers, a great pit of titan works, is sunk deep into the ground, and beside it stands a lonely watcher, Creteus, whom the frostborn call the keeper.', 'quest 12865 description (Foot Steppes east, hard land, rhino, proto-drakes); quest 12875 description (the keeper Creteus); quest 12877 description (Creteus keeping watch on the Engine of the Makers); quest 12878 description (Frigid Tomb to the southeast, ancient beings of ice); quest 12880 description (Norgannon''s Binding in the Engine of the Makers, the large pit beside us); zone_areas 4432 phase 1 (Ice Steppe Rhino, Stormpeak Wyrm, Stormforged Tracker, Creteus 30052), 4473 (Icebound Revenant)'),
(6709, 1, 67, 9, 0, 13, 'Bouldercrag''s Refuge and the Snowdrift Plains', 'Bouldercrag''s Refuge is an old titan building on the face of a mountain west of the Inventor''s Library, where the earthen expelled from Ulduar have taken shelter. On the Snowdrift Plains below they hold the line against Loken''s stormforged and their war golems, with dolomite giants fighting at their side. The irons gain ground inch by inch. Fallen defenders lie in the snow, and the earthen mine what enchanted earth they can from the cliffs to heal them.', 'quests 12885, 12929 descriptions (old titan building, west of the Inventor''s Library); quest 12930 description (craftsmen reborn as warriors; enchanted earth from the cliff face); quest 12931 description (losing ground inch by inch); quest 12937 description (fallen defenders); zone_areas 4436 (Earthen Defender, Fallen Earthen Defender, Dolomite Giant f1770, Stormforged Raider and Reaver, War Golem)'),
(6710, 1, 67, 10, 0, 13, 'Nidavelir and Narvir''s Cradle', 'Nidavelir is the stronghold of the stormforged iron dwarves, southwest across the Snowdrift Plains from Bouldercrag''s Refuge, and Runeseer Valduran commands there, said to hold powerful titan artifacts given him by Loken. On the western side of the plains the irons have dug the Frozen Mine, where captive mechagnomes, servants of Keeper Mimir, haul out cartloads of dark, sickly ore. South of the refuge sprawls Narvir''s Cradle, a great construction ground of scaffolds and lightning forges where stormforged artificers labor on a project of Valduran''s. Far to the south, Uldis, a titan facility, opens on a mountain above the Bor''s Breath River.', 'quest 12965 description (Runeseer Valduran; Keeper Loken''s artifacts; Nidavelir southwest across the plains); quests 12957, 12964 descriptions (Frozen Mine, captive mechagnomes of Keeper Mimir, dark sickly ore); quests 12988, 12991 descriptions (Narvir''s Cradle, large construction area to the south; lightning forges; artificers); quest 12998 description (Uldis, titan facility in the south above the Bor''s Breath River); zone_areas 4434, 4435 (Scaffold Cars, Lightning Forges, Stormforged Artificer)'),
(6711, 1, 67, 11, 0, 13, 'The Inventor''s Library', 'The Inventor''s Library stands on the northern coast south of Ulduar, built by Keeper Mimir, the tinker, to hold his work. Its guardians still murmur through diagnostics, data restoration and security protocols among the databanks, and a scrapbot, SCRAP-E, is charged with keeping the consoles in Mimir''s absence, though its last maintenance cycle is long overdue. East along the northern mountain face stands Mimir''s Workshop, unused for many years, where a few of the keeper''s attendants still wait for their next directive.', 'quest 12858 description (Inventor''s Library on the northern coast, south of Ulduar); quest 12927 description (Keeper Mimir, the tinker who built this library); creature_text 29724 (Library Guardian lines); quests 12888, 12889 (SCRAP-E; maintain consoles in Mimir''s absences; 489 days); quest 12980 description (Mimir''s Workshop east along the northern face; unused; attendants still functional); npc_text 13703 (Attendant Tock)'),
(6712, 1, 67, 12, 0, 13, 'The Valley of Ancient Winters', 'The Valley of Ancient Winters runs east from Brunnhildar Village toward Dun Niffelem, and it is the battlefield of their feud: Hyldnir warbears clash there with the frost giants of Niffelem and their frostworgs. Off the valley opens the Hibernal Cavern, where the Hyldnir long found their best bears, but ravenous jormungar have overrun it and the wild bears are all but gone. On a mountainside above the valley, a round door leads into a titan vault called Loken''s Bargain.', 'quest 12851 objectives (frostworgs and frost giants in the valley); quest 12856 description (Dun Niffelem east of the valley); quest 12983 description (Hibernal Cave, overrun by jormungar, wild bears all but extinct); quest 13274 description (vault called Loken''s Bargain, round entrance on a mountainside overlooking the valley); zone_areas 4437 phase 1 (Brunnhildar Warbear, Niffelem Frost Giant, Frostworg)'),
(6713, 1, 67, 13, 0, 13, 'Dun Niffelem', 'Dun Niffelem is the city of the frost giants who call themselves the Sons of Hodir, east of the Valley of Ancient Winters, where spikes of ice rise over the giants'' halls. The giants are at war with the Hyldnir: proto-drakes taken from Brunnhildar lie chained in the city, and captured Hyldnir warriors stand frozen in blocks of ice where the giants can mock them. The Sons of Hodir were once allies of Thorim, but they have long nursed a hatred of the Stormlord, and strangers are not welcome here lightly.', 'quest 12856 description (Dun Niffelem east of the valley; captive proto-drakes; sisters frozen in ice and taunted); quest 12924 description (soften their hatred of me); quest 12972 description (Thorim''s former allies); npc_text 13747 (Jokkum: permitted to visit; do not bring us dishonor); zone_areas 4438 phase 1 (Son of Hodir 29809, Brunnhildar Prisoner, Captive Proto-Drake)'),
(6714, 1, 67, 14, 0, 13, 'Fjorn''s Anvil and Frostfield Lake', 'East of Dun Niffelem glows Fjorn''s Anvil, the forge of Fjorn, who has laid siege to the frost giants'' city with giants of iron. The anvil is scalding even in the wintry air. Fire revenants, seething with heat, guard it and stalk the shores of Frostfield Lake, where stormforged iron giants march, and the frost giants of Niffelem can do little against them while Fjorn holds his anvil.', 'quest 12915 description (Fjorn has besieged Dun Niffelem with giants of iron; Fjorn''s Anvil east of Dun Niffelem); quest 12922 description and completion text (revenants at Frostfield Lake; anvil scalding); zone_areas 4495/4439 phase 1 (Fjorn 29503, Seething Revenant, Stormforged Iron Giant 29375)'),
(6715, 1, 67, 15, 0, 13, 'Thunderfall', 'Thunderfall lies northeast of Dun Niffelem, a desolate field of ice where frozen fossils lie half buried in the ground. Little stirs here but the wind and a few tundra rams, and among the fossils lies the body of a fallen frostborn warrior, far from his home. To the frost giants of Dun Niffelem, the place is bound up with a dark memory they have never let go.', 'quest 12975 description (Thunderfall northeast; frozen fossils a reminder of that dark day); zone_areas 4440 phase 1 (Tundra Ram, Fallen Frostborn Warrior 29976)'),
(6716, 1, 67, 16, 0, 13, 'Camp Tunka''lo', 'Camp Tunka''lo is a village of taunka in the far east of the peaks, beyond the Terrace of the Makers and north of Dun Niffelem, its tents guarded by the camp''s braves. Scrolls of the village''s history are kept about the camp. To the north lies the Howling Hollow, where the taunka bury their honored elders, and to the northwest Frostfloe Deep, the burial cave of their warriors. Below the camp spreads the Plain of Echoes, where mammoths and rhinos roam, scions of storm ride the wind and the restless spirits of taunka ancestors wander.', 'quest 13426 description (location); quest 13034 description (history scrolls throughout the camp); quest 13049 description (Howling Hollow north, elders'' burial); quest 13037 description (Frostfloe Deep northwest, burial cave of the warriors); zone_areas 4441 (Tunka''lo Braves, History Scrolls 192493-192495), 4444 (Plains Mammoth, Romping Rhino, Scion of Storm, Disturbed Taunka Ancestor)'),
(6717, 1, 67, 17, 0, 13, 'The Terrace of the Makers', 'The Terrace of the Makers spreads over the high ground northwest of Dun Niffelem toward Ulduar, the sacred grounds of the titans. Temples crown its heights: the Temple of Invention, seat of Keeper Mimir, with the Temples of Winter, Life and Order, and beyond them the Hall of the Shaper and the Temple of Wisdom, the last just southwest of Ulduar. The terrace is a battlefield. Loken''s iron dwarves burst from the ground in mole machines with iron sentinels beside them, and the earthen, sworn to guard these grounds with their lives, fight on against them.', 'quest 13057 objectives (terrace northwest of Dun Niffelem); npc_text 13802 (Thorim sworn to protect the Terrace of the Makers); quest 13285 description (Temple of Invention, seat of Keeper Mimir); quest 12986 objectives (Temples of Invention, Winter, Life, Order); quest 13035 description (Hall of the Shaper); quest 13047 description (Temple of Wisdom, southwest of Ulduar); quest 13005 description (earthen oath to protect these grounds with their lives); zone_areas 4446 (Iron Dwarf Assailant and Magus, Iron Dwarf Mole Machine, Iron Sentinel, Earthen Elite and Warder)'),
(6718, 1, 67, 18, 0, 13, 'Ulduar', 'Ulduar rises at the northern edge of the Storm Peaks, a titan city of colossal halls, towers and gates, and Loken holds it now. Its earthen makers live in exile, and from its outer works open the Halls of Stone and the Halls of Lightning. On the approach to the city, a trader named Chester Copperpot keeps a camp of general and trade goods under the watch of his hired goons, Slosh sells food and drink beside him, and Shavalius the Fancy keeps a flight master''s post for travelers.', 'quest 12929 description (the earthen who built and maintained Ulduar, ousted when Loken took over); zone_areas 4445 (Chester Copperpot 32477 General & Trade Supplies, Copperpot Goon 32476, Slosh 32478 Food & Drink, Shavalius the Fancy 29951 flight master); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Chester_Copperpot (added 3.0.2)'),
(6730, 2, 67, 0, 0, 13, 'Thorim', 'Thorim, the Stormlord, is a being of near godlike stature who served the titans as guardian of Ulduar and the Terrace of the Makers. Now he sits alone in the Temple of Storms, sunk in a grief so deep that he barely heeds those who climb to him, while far below the Hyldnir compete in the Hyldsmeet for the honor of a lifetime at his side. What broke him he does not tell to strangers.', 'npc_text 13778 (near godlike stature; guardian of Ulduar and the Terrace of the Makers); npc_text 13540 (Hyldsmeet victory assures a lifetime next to Thorim); quest 12886 completion and reward text'),
(6731, 2, 67, 1, 0, 13, 'Loken', 'Loken is the master of Ulduar, a keeper of the titans who has taken the city for himself. When he seized it he expelled the earthen who had built and tended it, and he sent his favorite servants, the iron dwarves, on a brutal campaign against all the creatures of stone. They have hunted the exiles relentlessly ever since, and wherever the stormforged march across the peaks, they march in his name.', 'quest 12885 description (Loken''s favorite servants; brutal campaign; expelled the earthen); quest 12929 description (ousted when Loken took over the city; relentless attacks on the exiles); quest 12965 description (Keeper Loken, who took over Ulduar); npc_text 14203 (Loken''s minions)'),
(6732, 2, 67, 2, 0, 13, 'Brann Bronzebeard', 'Brann Bronzebeard, the famed explorer of the Explorers'' League and a brother of King Magni of Ironforge, has come to the Storm Peaks on the trail of Ulduar, and no one quite knows where he is. The secrets of the titans have drawn him north across Northrend, and his own notes point to these mountains. Those who would find him, friend or not, must start from his camp at the foot of titan ruins above the frozen Bor''s Breath River.', 'quest 12854 description (Brann''s camp across the Bor''s Breath River at the foot of ruins of the Path of the Titans); quest 12895 description (his journal entries; campsite overlooking the frozen Bor''s Breath River); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Brann_Bronzebeard (Explorers'' League, brother of Magni)'),
(6733, 2, 67, 3, 0, 13, 'King Jokkum', 'King Jokkum rules the Sons of Hodir from Dun Niffelem, a frost giant who listens patiently and weighs every request before he answers. The death of Fjorn earned its bringer a hearing, but the bad blood between his people and Thorim runs deep, and his first answer to the Stormlord''s envoy was a measured one: as payment for the help against Fjorn, he let Njormeld reforge the armor the giants gave Thorim ages ago, and no more.', 'quest 12966 description; npc_text 13747 (do not bring us dishonor)'),
(6734, 2, 67, 4, 0, 13, 'Bouldercrag the Rockshaper', 'Bouldercrag the Rockshaper leads the earthen driven out of Ulduar, holding out at the refuge that bears his name. He remembers when his people''s hammers hewed stone instead of iron; since their expulsion the weakest of them have died and the strongest craftsmen have been reborn as warriors. His defenders are hardy but not tireless, and he counts every one who falls, yet the hammers of the earthen stand united behind him, and any friend of the earthen is welcome at his side.', 'quest 12930 description; quest 12931 description (hardy, but not tireless); quest 12937 description (every casualty is one too many); npc_text 14203 (Bruor: the hammers of the earthen stand united behind Bouldercrag); npc_text 13740 (welcome as a friend and ally of the earthen)'),
(6735, 2, 67, 5, 0, 13, 'Ricket', 'Ricket is a goblin of K3 with a grin for every explosion and a plan for every problem, most of them loud. She keeps the town''s sapper squad ready, lays Jeer Sparksocket''s new mines in the path of the magnataur of Garm, and sends newcomers out for food, for K3 has grown more popular than anyone planned for. She thinks herself brilliant and is never shy about saying so, and even Jeer warns that she is a little loopy.', 'quest 12827 description (food shortage; K3 got popular); quests 12820, 12821, 12826 (mines; sapper squad; Jeer: she''s a little loopy); quest 12828 completion text (my plan was brilliant); npc_text 13795'),
(6736, 2, 67, 6, 1, 13, 'Creteus', 'Creteus keeps watch over the Engine of the Makers from the Foot Steppes, the one the frostborn call the keeper. He speaks with grave courtesy and favors visitors who use their tongues before their blades, a quality he finds ever rarer among mortals. The hermit Drom Frostgrip spoke with him often and believed that what Creteus left unsaid gave away the secrets he guarded. He helps no one blindly, and asks first what a seeker truly wants.', 'quest 12875 description (Drom speaks to the keeper Creteus often); quest 12877 description, completion and reward text (omissions give him away; tongue over blade; on what business); quest 12986 description (unsure the seeker knows the purpose of what is sought)'),
(6737, 2, 67, 7, 2, 13, 'Xarantaur', 'Xarantaur calls himself the Witness. He was among the first tauren druids, of the last generation taught by Cenarius when the world was young, and where his kin hunted great beasts he hunted stories. He has come to Camp Tunka''lo to learn more of Stormhoof, a taunka hero whose battle against the North Wind he heard of from Wind Tamer Barah in the Borean Tundra, but the people of Tunka''lo seem to know nothing of him.', 'npc_text 14119, 14120 (the Witness; first tauren druids; taught by Cenarius; hunted stories); quest 13034 description (Barah''s tale; Tunka''lo know nothing of Stormhoof); quest 13426 description and reward text'),
(6740, 3, 67, 0, 0, 13, 'The Hyldsmeet', 'Deep in the Forlorn Mine, chained among the Hyldnir''s captives, sits Lok''lira the Crone, who says that among her people she is known as a Yrkvinn, a weaver of illusions. She guesses at once that a stranger has come for the goblin prisoner, Zeev Fizzlespark, and offers a bargain. No one will get him out by force, not alive, but with her runes she could make her rescuer pass unnoticed among the Hyldnir. The runes are in the keeping of Overseer Syra, who patrols the mine, and Lok''lira says she dreads what will become of her if she stays a prisoner much longer.', 'quest 12846 reward text; quest 12841 description and reward text'),
(6741, 3, 67, 1, 0, 13, 'The Stormlord''s Atonement', 'Roused at last, Thorim means to take back the Terrace of the Makers from his brother, but he cannot do it alone, and the allies he needs are the ones he wronged. As a first step toward mending fences with the frost giants of Dun Niffelem, he would strike at their common enemy: Fjorn, whose giants of iron besiege the giants'' city from Fjorn''s Anvil in the east. To his envoy he gives a charm that calls his earthen to fight alongside.', 'quest 12915 description; quest 13064 reward text (assist me in setting these wrongs to right)'),
(6742, 3, 67, 2, 0, 13, 'The Reckoning', 'With his armor restored, Thorim prepares to strike at his brother''s army, and for that he needs a mount. Years ago he released his riding drake, Veranus, into the wild, and she returned to lead her own brood. She is long past breeding now, but out of sheer pride she still guards her old, empty nest. Thorim has a plan to bring her back, if someone will steal him eggs from the other proto-drake nests near Brunnhildar and set them where she will see.', 'quest 13050 description; quest 13009 reward text (much to be done); quest 13051 description'),
(6743, 3, 67, 3, 0, 13, 'The Sons of Hodir', 'The frost giants of Dun Niffelem call themselves the Sons of Hodir, and they look to Hodir for protection and guidance. Outsiders earn their regard slowly, by deeds. Their smith Njormeld has drawn up plans for an artifact that will bring Hodir''s blessing of protection to the stronghold, and needs only the eyes of their fallen iron foes to finish it. The giants treasure everfrost, ice that never melts, as the symbol of their people''s heart, though over the ages the jormungar have devoured nearly all of it.', 'quest 12985 description; quest 13420 description and reward text (everfrost, symbol of the heart of our people; jormungar devoured it)'),
(6744, 3, 67, 4, 0, 13, 'The Iron Colossus', 'The stormforged war golems of Nidavelir wear plates of armor too thick and too large for them, bolted on like a crude upgrade, and the earthen can hardly bear the metal: even its presence brings Bruor Ironbane pain. Runeseer Valduran has spent an extraordinary effort mining, refining, smithing and testing it. Bruor suspects one of the runeseer''s schemes and wants to know what the plates are really for, and whether the attendants of Mimir''s old workshop can still tell him.', 'quest 12979 description and reward text; quest 12980 description'),
(6745, 3, 67, 5, 0, 13, 'Norgannon''s Keystone', 'Brann Bronzebeard has a lead on Norgannon''s keystone, which guards the way into Ulduar''s archives. The titans split it in two and hid the halves. The first, the keystone''s shell, is held in the Inventor''s Library, Keeper Mimir''s hall on the northern coast south of Ulduar, and it is reached with an inventor''s disk assembled from fragments the library''s guardians carry. Brann works through his communicator while he hunts for the other half himself, and he guides each step from afar.', 'quest 12858 description (keystone, archives, two pieces, shell in the Inventor''s Library, disk fragments from the guardians); npc_text 14089; quest 12927 description (Keeper Mimir; I''ll be tracking down the other half of the archive key)'),
(6746, 3, 67, 6, 1, 13, 'The Brothers Bronzebeard', 'Yorg Stormheart, King of the Frostborn, is held by his people to be the wisest and strongest leader they have known, and he has trained them into fearsome warriors. His peachy skin sets him apart from those he rules. Lagnus of the Explorers'' League urges courtesy toward him, for he is deeply respected. The king will not force his people into outsiders'' affairs, but he offers the League their aid if its champion proves as strong and fierce as any frostborn.', 'quest 12864 reward text (wisest and strongest leader; peachy skin); quest 12873 description (very respected); quest 12874 description');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(6701, 1, 0, 255, 'A runner set a teleporter up behind Garm, on Garm''s Rise, and once its lost power cell had been found and fitted, the way into the magnataur''s lair lay open. Gino''s goblin sappers now hold the rise and fight in Garm itself, and the brutes have nowhere left to run.', 'quest 12821 description and reward text; quest 12822 description (sappers back you up; nowhere to run); spell_area 54635 in 4421/4461; Gino 29432 and Goblin Sapper 29555 in phase 2'),
(6701, 2, 0, 255, 'Gino''s masterpiece, a hardpacked explosive bundle weeks in the making, was planted beside Frostgut''s Altar at the back of the magnataur cave. Tormar Frostgut died there and the whole mountain shook, and Gino, whom the Inventor''s League mocks because his inventions all blow up, could not have been prouder.', 'quest 12823 description and reward text'),
(6702, 1, 0, 255, 'The captured goblin men have been freed and are back with Gretchen Fizzlespark, all but one. Her brother Zeev, the others say, is still up in the village, and the Hyldnir keep a mine where they put their prisoners to work.', 'quest 12843 reward text; quest 12846 description'),
(6703, 1, 0, 255, 'Wrapped in Lok''lira''s illusion, a stranger passes for a battle-sister, and the village opens its doors. Lodge-Matron Embla offers food and rest, Gretta the Arbiter keeps the order of the contests, Astrid Bjornrittar breaks bears for riding, and Iva the Vengeful and Thyra Kvinnshal rage against Valkyrion, whose Hyldnir took the Lich King''s offer when Brunnhildar dismembered his emissaries.', 'spell_area 55012, 72914 from accepting 12905; quest 12841 description (her runes would let you go unnoticed among them); npc_text 13663 (Embla), 13843 (Gretta), 13785 (Astrid), 14033 (Iva); quests 12925 and 12942 descriptions'),
(6704, 1, 0, 255, 'Yulda the Stormspeaker has paid for insulting the Hyldsmeet. A blade sent by Iva the Vengeful found her in the largest dwelling of Valkyrion, and in Brunnhildar they say she had it coming: no one mocks their traditions and lives, not even one of their own.', 'quest 12968 description and reward text'),
(6706, 1, 0, 255, 'King Stormheart has told his people that he will be leaving them for a time, and he was firm that none of the frostborn should follow him. They respect his wishes, as they always have. Velog Icebellow has taken charge of the clan in his absence, and Frosthold''s welcome to its friends still stands.', 'quest 12973 reward text (off to settle a score); npc_text 13764 (Velog: taking his leave; grim memory; insisted we not join him; I have taken responsibility for our clan)'),
(6708, 1, 0, 255, 'When Norgannon''s Core was lifted from the Frigid Tomb, the steppes erupted. An iron host poured across them, stormforged warmongers and iron behemoths among them, and King Yorg Stormheart and his frostborn axemen met it on the open ground, with Creteus standing among them above the Engine of the Makers.', 'quest 12879 description (footsteps, battle in the distance); spell_area 55782 (Spell.dbc aura 261, phase 2) in 4431/4432/4473 from accepting 12879 until 12973 is taken; phase 2 spawns 30182, 30065, 30064, 30060, 30082'),
(6710, 1, 0, 255, 'Loken''s gifts to Valduran, the relics called Loken''s Fury, Loken''s Power and Loken''s Favor, have been destroyed in Nidavelir, and the stormforged are weaker for it. They fight on all the same: their own losses mean nothing to them, and Bouldercrag fears they will keep coming until the earthen are pounded to gravel.', 'quest 12965 objectives and reward text'),
(6712, 1, 0, 255, 'To Thorim''s envoy the valley shows another face. The Sons of Hodir walk it openly, stoic mammoths graze its floor, wild wyrms circle overhead and jormungar roam the snow, and the carcasses of icemaw bears lie where the jormungar left them.', 'spell_area 55858 (phase 4) from accepting 12924; phase 4 spawns in 4437: 30262, 30260, 30275, 30422, 30292'),
(6713, 1, 0, 255, 'To Thorim''s envoy the city opens its halls. King Jokkum holds court here with Lorekeeper Randvir and the frostworg denmother close by, Lillehoff serves as the giants'' quartermaster and Calder sells smithing supplies, and in the stronghold looms the frozen image of Arngrim the Insatiable, the old king of the giants.', 'spell_area 55858 from accepting 12924; phase 4 spawns 30105, 30252, 30294, 32540, 32594, gameobject 192524; quest 13046 description (Arngrim''s legendary hunger; the old king)'),
(6713, 2, 0, 255, 'Fjorn''s great anvil has been cooled and carried home from the east, and it stands in Dun Niffelem now beside Njormeld, the giant sent to recover it, who means to put it to work for his people.', 'quest 12966 description (Njormeld sent to recover Fjorn''s anvil); quest 12967 reward text; spell_area 55952, 56771 from 12967 rewarded; gameobject 192071 and Njormeld 30127 in phase 8'),
(6714, 1, 0, 255, 'Since Fjorn fell, the iron giants lie dead on the fields by Frostfield Lake, and the Sons of Hodir have come to claim his anvil. Njormeld oversees the work while frost giant stormheralds breathe cold over its glowing face, cooling it so that it can be carried home.', 'quest 12966 description (Njormeld sent to recover the anvil); quest 12967 description (cooling Fjorn''s anvil so it can be taken home); spell_area 55858, 61209; Frost Giant Stormherald 30121 (aura 56568 Cooling Breath), Dead Iron Giant 29914/30163'),
(6714, 2, 0, 255, 'The anvil has been cooled at last and carried away to its new home. Where it stood, the ground is cluttered with smoldering scraps of iron, the shrapnel of the battle fought here, and fire revenants still stalk among them, seething with the old heat.', 'quest 12967 reward text; spell_area 55952 from 12967 rewarded; Smoldering Scrap Bunny 30169 and Seething Revenant 30387 in phase 8'),
(6715, 1, 0, 255, 'Thunderfall is not at rest. To those who come in Thorim''s cause, the spirits of Niffelem forefathers and of frostborn warriors are plain to see, wandering restless among the ice, and the shattered fragments of a great horn lie scattered in the snow.', 'spell_area 55858 from accepting 12924; phase 4 spawns 29974, 30135, 30144; gameobject 192081 phase 4; quest 12975 description (spirits haunt that place; fragments of Hodir''s Horn)'),
(6715, 2, 0, 255, 'Sounded over the fallen of Thunderfall, the ethereal echo of Hodir''s Horn lays the tormented spirits to rest and leaves a sense of peace behind it. It does not last: in time they rise again, and the horn must be blown anew.', 'quest 12977 description, completion and reward text (a daily quest)'),
(6717, 1, 0, 255, 'Loken had not left the terrace to his iron dwarves alone. His most powerful lieutenants held it for him, and Thorim''s champion hunted them down with the earthen at the call of the Horn of the Peaks: the giant Eisenfaust in the Hall of the Shaper, then Halefnir the Windborn and Duronn the Runewrought deeper within. One by one, Loken''s servants fell.', 'quest 13035 description and reward text; creature_template 30341, 30353, 30376 (subname Servant of Loken)'),
(6718, 1, 14, 255, 'In time the way into Ulduar opened to the bold. Brann Bronzebeard has led an expedition to the city''s gates, where engineers of the Explorers'' League and K3 have rebuilt siege engines left by the Alliance and Horde expeditions that came before them. Archmage Pentarus, who helped fund the venture, and the mages of the Kirin Tor shield their platform. What waits within is for those who follow to learn.', 'mod-individual-progression: Ulduar opens at state 14 (PROGRESSION_WOTLK_TIER_1); Ulduar raid (patch 3.1), map 603 entrance: npc_text 14369 (Brann 33579: siege machines rebuilt from the Alliance and Horde expeditions before us), 14362 (Archmage Pentarus 33624: Brann asked me to help fund this expedition); creature_text 33624 group 1 (mages of the Kirin Tor, release the shield, defend this platform), 33579 group 0; map 603 spawns: Hired Engineer (Explorer''s League), Hired Demolitionist (K3), High Explorer Dellorah'),
(6730, 1, 0, 255, 'Thorim''s grief is for his wife, Sif, slain by his own brother. He was sworn to guard the pacts between the races of frost as well as the titans'' grounds, yet his brother tricked him into blaming Sif''s death on a dear friend, Arngrim, king of the frost giants, and he turned on his allies. When he saw what he had done, he gave in to despair. Now he means to avenge Sif and free the titans'' sacred grounds from his brother''s madness.', 'npc_text 13801, 13802, 13803 (Thorim''s gossip, shown only while 13064 is in the log); quest 13064 description and reward text'),
(6731, 1, 0, 255, 'At the Temple of Wisdom, Loken revealed a deeper deceit. Lok''lira the Crone, the frail prisoner of the Forlorn Mine who set Thorim''s awakening in motion, was his illusion. He had waited for weeks in that mine for a champion bold enough to rouse his brother and draw him away from the Temple of Storms, where Thorim was strongest, to fight close to the power of Loken''s own master.', 'creature_text 30396 groups 4, 6, 7 (fight closer to my master''s power; I waited for you for weeks inside that Hyldnir mine; the shape wasn''t mine)'),
(6732, 1, 0, 255, 'His camp was found deserted, iron dwarves prowling where he had worked and only a note left behind. A tracking beast followed the scent from the camp to his stolen belongings and his communicator, and through it Brann himself appeared, alive and plainly surprised to see who had found him.', 'quests 12855, 12910 descriptions and reward text; quests 12854, 12895 reward text (only a note); zone_areas 4476 Abandoned Camp (Stormforged Tracker)'),
(6732, 2, 0, 255, 'Once Moteha''s wind magic let them understand each other, Brann spoke bluntly. He knew Scout Vor''takh''s reputation and guessed he was to be abducted, but he had greater worries: the titans'' creations are at war, Loken has taken Ulduar, and if Horde and Alliance spend themselves on each other, Loken will destroy them both. Boktar Bloodfury heeded him and chose to help.', 'creature_text 29579 groups 0-9; quest 12917 reward text; quest 12920 reward text (Vor''takh''s plan is not the way of the Horde; it serves us to help him)'),
(6733, 1, 0, 255, 'Jokkum remembers the dark day at Thunderfall that divides his people from Thorim. The frozen fossils there and the spirits that haunt the place keep it alive, and he believes his people will never forgive the Stormlord until something takes the place of those images: a memorial, built from the shattered pieces of Hodir''s Horn.', 'quests 12975, 12976 descriptions'),
(6733, 2, 0, 255, 'When word came of the fight near Ulduar, Jokkum would not believe it at first. No one could defeat Thorim in single combat, he cried, not a giant nor a beast, least of all his coward of a brother. On his forefathers'' names he swore that Loken would pay.', 'quest 13047 reward text'),
(6734, 1, 0, 255, 'Those who come to the refuge in Brann Bronzebeard''s name find a warm welcome. Bouldercrag counts the explorer the closest ally his people have among those of flesh, a brother to the earthen in their struggle against Loken and his followers and in the fight to win back Ulduar.', 'quests 12885, 12929 reward text'),
(6734, 2, 0, 255, 'Bouldercrag could not even touch the dark ore the irons haul from the Frozen Mine. It seethes with an unnatural energy no creature of stone can bear, and he was left to wonder what the stormforged meant to make of it.', 'quest 12964 reward text'),
(6734, 3, 0, 255, 'Bouldercrag greeted the colossus''s fall with joy, but he knew the victory would not hold on its own. Brann had to be warned before Loken thought to rebuild his forces, and the only way to make the day last, he said, was to go into Ulduar and defeat Loken for all time.', 'quest 13007 reward text; creature_text 29801 groups 0-1'),
(6735, 1, 0, 255, 'Even Ricket admits that K3 will not win a foothold deeper in the peaks: freezing engines, vrykul women, territorial drakes and half a dozen other nasties have seen to that. One-way trips are another matter, and her rockets, the D16 Propelled Delivery Devices, fling the willing over the mountains.', 'quests 12862, 13060 descriptions and objectives'),
(6736, 1, 0, 255, 'Creteus is troubled. He has learned that the seat of the watcher Thorim is contested and his fate uncertain, and the databank he sent to the temples of the Terrace of the Makers found the other watchers gone from them. What befell them he cannot say, but he fears their absence spells dark times for all of Azeroth.', 'quest 12986 description, objectives and reward text'),
(6736, 2, 0, 255, 'When iron dwarves came after Norgannon''s Core, Creteus understood what their numbers meant. Someone is using the Forge of Wills to make an army, and Ulduar, he says, is no longer safe.', 'quest 12879 completion and reward text'),
(6737, 1, 0, 255, 'Tunka''lo''s own scrolls told Stormhoof''s tale differently, as a villain''s, and the Lorehammer that Nozdormu gave Xarantaur when the bronze dragonflight made him immortal stirred at it: time has gone awry here. Even the spirit of Chieftain Swiftspear, Stormhoof''s brother, is losing his memories of the hero, and the Witness means to restore the true history.', 'quest 13034 reward text; creature_text 30381 group 7 (hero, not a villain), 10-11; quest 13037 description and reward text; creature_text 30395 groups 3-4'),
(6737, 2, 0, 255, 'The North Wind was behind it. Weakened long ago by Stormhoof, it had bided its time and set its minions to rewrite Tunka''lo''s history and destroy the spirits of its honored dead. Sent back by the Lorehammer to fight the North Wind in Stormhoof''s own shape, a champion saw the hero fall as history required, then took up the Horn of Elemental Fury he dropped and destroyed the North Wind. Stormhoof''s story was restored.', 'creature_text 30381 groups 1-5; quest 13058 description and reward text'),
(6740, 1, 0, 255, 'Wearing her illusion, the stranger served Mildred the Cruel as a new overseer, driving exhausted vrykul men back to work and slaying Garhal, who had been stirring talk of revolt. Satisfied, Mildred handed over the key to the shackles of a troublesome prisoner, to be quietly killed: Lok''lira herself, whose crime was to claim a place in the Hyldsmeet.', 'quests 12905, 12906, 12907, 12908 descriptions and reward text'),
(6740, 2, 0, 255, 'In Brunnhildar, Zeev was about to be torn apart by Agnetta Tyrsdottar, and taking his place won his freedom and an entry into the Hyldsmeet, the contest that decides who will rule at Thorim''s side. Then Lok''lira told her purpose: Thorim lost his wife to his brother''s treachery and turned on the frost giants, and she wants him roused to retake Ulduar before the world is torn asunder.', 'quests 12969, 12970 descriptions and reward text; npc_text 13778, 13779, 13780; creature_text 29525'),
(6740, 3, 0, 255, 'Beating six victorious challengers was not enough, for the Hyldnir give warbears only to those proven in true battle. Riding Brijana''s bear Icefang through the Valley of Ancient Winters, the newcomer rained death on frostworgs and frost giants, then freed a captive proto-drake in Dun Niffelem and used it to carry home sisters frozen in the giants'' ice.', 'quests 12971, 12972, 12851, 12856, 13063 descriptions and reward text'),
(6740, 4, 0, 255, 'Astrid Bjornrittar made a bear rider of the newcomer: a harness of yeti hide, an icemaw matriarch rescued from the jormungar of the Hibernal Cavern, a bout against the chained yeti Kirgaraak, and at last victory over the warbears of the Pit of the Fang, though the matriarch came out of it badly hurt.', 'quests 12900, 12983, 12996, 12997 descriptions and reward text'),
(6740, 5, 0, 255, 'Before the last trial Lok''lira tied a thin strand of hair into the champion''s own. In the Drakkensryd, riders battle on proto-drakes around the Temple of Storms with chained harpoons, and the newcomer won it. Thorim looked up from his grief at the victor and, for a moment, spoke a name: Sif.', 'quest 13062 description (thin strand of hair); quest 12886 description and reward text (Sif... is that you?); npc_text 13801 (that strand of hair)'),
(6741, 1, 0, 255, 'Among the wreckage of Fjorn''s iron giants lay a strange, slag-covered metal, and the anvil''s fire, fed with sparks torn from the revenants, burned it clean: hard but not brittle, far lighter than it looked, and marked with one of Thorim''s runes. It was what remained of his own armor, cast off in grief long ago, and only the Sons of Hodir who made it could reforge it.', 'item 41556 Slag Covered Metal (drops from Stormforged Iron Giant 29375, starts 12922); quests 12922, 12956 descriptions and reward text; quest 12924 description'),
(6741, 2, 0, 255, 'Njormeld did the work on Fjorn''s own anvil once it had been cooled and carried home. The new suit was finer than the old and took less metal to make, whether by Njormeld''s skill or by the truth of the anvil''s legends, and the giants sent it to Thorim as a reminder of the days when they stood together, invincible.', 'quests 12966, 12967 descriptions; quest 12924 reward text; quest 13009 description'),
(6741, 3, 0, 255, 'Forgiveness needed more than armor. The fragments of Hodir''s Horn were gathered from Thunderfall and brought to Njormeld, whose eyes grew moist as he poured them onto his anvil: the horn was a sacred gift to his people from Hodir himself. From its pieces he will raise a monument, meant to soothe the pain the giants have borne so long and bring them back to Thorim''s side.', 'quests 12975, 12976 descriptions and reward text'),
(6741, 4, 0, 255, 'Summoned by Jokkum, Thorim came and begged forgiveness for the harm his grief had done, and the king granted it: that dark day would never be spoken of again. Then Jokkum returned what Thorim thought lost, Krolmir, the Hammer of Storms, hurled to the earth that day. As the blast filled the land, Jokkum''s father Arngrim had cast a rune upon it to keep it from their enemies, his final act.', 'quest 13010 description and reward text; creature_text 30331 groups 1-8, 30390 groups 0-3'),
(6742, 1, 0, 255, 'The stolen eggs were laid in her nest, and Veranus came down roaring to defend it. Thorim dropped onto her back from above and mastered her once more, calling her his old friend, and for the first time in years he felt his luck turning.', 'creature_text 30461, 30462; quest 13051 reward text'),
(6742, 2, 0, 255, 'On the Terrace of the Makers, Thorim owned that he had neglected his duty for years while the earthen kept their oath to guard those grounds with their lives. With the Horn of the Peaks he rallied them, and together they threw back the iron dwarves and iron sentinels. It was a good start, he said, but his brother''s forces would soon regroup.', 'quest 13005 description and reward text'),
(6742, 3, 0, 255, 'Thorim called Loken out near the Temple of Wisdom and fought him alone, as he had sworn, with only a witness beside him. He had the better of his brother until Loken turned the fight with treachery, and at Loken''s word his minions carried off the Stormlord and Veranus to new dwellings, Loken having some special purpose in mind for the broodmother.', 'quest 13047 description; creature_text 30399 groups 0-5, 30396 groups 0-5'),
(6743, 1, 0, 255, 'The helm was forged and raised: Hodir''s Helm now crowns an ice spike in Dun Niffelem, and with it the stronghold will be warned of danger before it arrives. The honor of reading its pronouncement to the king and his people went to an outsider, a thing never granted before.', 'quest 12985 reward text; quest 12987 description and reward text; spell_area 56773'),
(6743, 2, 0, 255, 'Lorekeeper Randvir received a vision from Hodir himself revealing the secret of a great artifact, and warned that doom would follow if the gift were refused. From everfrost shards gathered in the depths of the Hibernal Cavern and the hides of stoic mammoths, Hodir''s Spear was raised in Dun Niffelem, a prophecy fulfilled.', 'quest 13001 description and reward text; spell_area 56772 (see invisibility 8) from 13001 rewarded shows Hodir''s Spear 192079'),
(6743, 3, 0, 255, 'The giants'' old king is not forgotten either. The frozen image of Arngrim the Insatiable still wears a look of famished yearning, for in life nothing ever sated him. Fed the spirits of jormungar from the valley, the old king''s hunger seems to ease, though only for now.', 'quest 13046 description and reward text (a daily quest)'),
(6744, 1, 0, 255, 'Attendant Tock found the plate to be saronite alloyed with iron, from ore that came from deep in the crust of Azeroth and could only have been made by a powerful, malevolent force. Its records were sealed in Ulduar''s archives by order of Keeper Loken, but the plate''s size and bolt holes spoke plainly: armor for something colossal, meant for the final strike against the refuge.', 'creature_text 30190 groups 0-9; quest 12980 reward text'),
(6744, 2, 0, 255, 'Valduran the Stormborn was hunted down in Nidavelir, with Bouldercrag and Bruor fighting at his attacker''s side, and he died there. Before he fell he scoffed at the earthen and boasted that nothing they did could prevent the completion of the iron colossus.', 'quest 12984 description and reward text; creature_text 29368, 30152 groups 0-1'),
(6744, 3, 0, 255, 'The lightning forges of Narvir''s Cradle were wrecked and its artificers cut down, but the plans taken there showed a colossus nearly done, lacking only the Heart of the Storm, kept in the titan facility of Uldis. Overseer Narvir reached it first, and with the heart in his hands the colossus would come to its full power.', 'quests 12988, 12991, 12993 descriptions and reward text; quest 12998 description and reward text'),
(6744, 4, 0, 255, 'With no way left to stop it, the earthen met the colossus on the Snowdrift Plains with Bruor''s plan: whatever its armor, a jormungar''s acid could eat through it. Driven by an ally of the refuge, a jormungar tamed by the earthen handlers brought the iron colossus down, and the refuge was saved.', 'quest 13007 description and reward text; creature_text 30152 group 2'),
(6745, 1, 0, 255, 'The disk came out blank, but carried among the library''s databanks it filled with Mimir''s hidden data, and the library''s console greeted it as Keeper Mimir himself. Charged, the disk woke Archivist Mechaton, guardian of the shell, and the first half of the keystone was taken from it.', 'quests 12860/12927, 13415/13416, 12872/12928 descriptions and reward text'),
(6745, 2, 0, 255, 'The core was harder to find. Lagnus read its shape from the shell, King Stormheart''s challenge led to the hermit Drom Frostgrip, and Drom''s ring won a hearing from Creteus. Satisfied that Brann sought the keystone for a worthy end, and perhaps was the very one it was made for, Creteus named its resting place, the Frigid Tomb, and the core was found there in a sealed chest.', 'quests 12871, 12873, 12874, 12875, 12877, 12878 descriptions and reward text'),
(6745, 3, 0, 255, 'The Explorers'' League camp that bore Brann''s name had been ruined by iron dwarves, but the prospectors'' maps and notes survived. Soren''s notes named the core''s keeper, Athan, one of Mimir''s creations, in a vault now called Loken''s Bargain above the Valley of Ancient Winters, and the core was won from him.', 'quests 13273, 13274 descriptions and reward text'),
(6745, 4, 0, 255, 'Shell and core were joined at last, with Brann himself there to see it, and Norgannon''s keystone was whole. The key to Ulduar''s archives, which he had chased across the peaks, was in his hands, and Brann could hardly contain his excitement at what might wait within.', 'quest 12973 description; quest 13285 description and reward text; creature_text 31810 groups 0-2'),
(6746, 1, 0, 255, 'Velog Icebellow told the tale on the way to the test. Years ago, frostborn crossing from the Dragonblight in a terrible blizzard found a mountain dwarf wandering in bloodied snow with no memory of his name. When a jormungar struck, the stranger grew, his skin turned to stone and lightning sizzled at his hands, and he slew it with a hurled hammer. They named him Yorg, a name kept for champions of legend.', 'creature_text 30401 groups 2-9'),
(6746, 2, 0, 255, 'At Frosthold, Brann Bronzebeard knew the king at once: Yorg Stormheart was his brother Muradin, long thought dead. His memories began to return, and King Magni, who had come to Northrend to find him, greeted him there. Muradin remembered Arthas, and how he had watched the prince turn and done nothing, and he set out alone to make Arthas answer for what he has done.', 'creature_text 30405, 30408 groups 0-13, 30411; quest 12973 reward text; npc_text 13764');
